==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=normality}}

===Etymology===
{{suffix|normal|ity}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ælɪti}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|normalities}}

# {{context|uncountable|lang=en}} The state of being [[normal]] or [[usual]]; [[normalcy]].
#:''Jessie was going to wear pants to school, but her brother persuaded her to wear shorts to preserve '''normality'''.''
# {{context|chemistry|lang=en}} The [[concentration]] of a [[solution]] expressed in [[gram equivalent weight]]s of [[solute]] per [[litre]] of [[solution]].
# {{context|countable|mathematics|statistics|lang=en}} A [[measure]] of how well an observed [[distribution]] approximates a [[normal distribution]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|state of being normal}} [[normalcy]] {{qualifier|US}}

====Antonyms====
* [[abnormality]]

